  "answer": "We should balance a chemical equation because of the law of conservation of mass. This law states that the total mass of the products formed in a chemical reaction must be equal to the total mass of the reactants consumed. Since atoms are the smallest particles involved in a chemical reaction and account for the mass of any substance, the number of atoms of each element must remain the same before and after the reaction. Therefore, balancing a chemical equation ensures that the number of atoms of each element is equal on both sides of the equation, reflecting the conservation of mass.",
